From 50456769967829050b0e23ebde505420b496a8a1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Gross <jason@theorem.dev>
Date: Tue, 22 Jul 2026 05:20:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm: restore pop {todo} for a softfp float/double passed in
 core registers

Follow-up to the two copy_params patches (derive gfunc_call's stack cleanup,
and rebuild the pop {todo} core-register mask from copy_params' own type_size).
Those two rebuild the pop {todo} bitmap inline -- discarding assign_regs'
*todo out-parameter, which MesCC returns short for a by-value struct -- but
they only rebuild it in the VT_STRUCT arm of CORE_STRUCT_CLASS. A softfp
`float`/`double` assigned to core registers is ALSO CORE_STRUCT_CLASS, yet it
takes the is_float vpush path (it has no VT_STRUCT store to hang the rebuild
on), so its words were never recorded. With the incoming *todo discarded and
no rebuild, todo stayed 0 for such a parameter and no `pop {todo}` was emitted:
the value was vpush'd to the stack and r0-r3 were never loaded. A call passing
two or more doubles (e.g. `pick1(1.5, 2.25)`) therefore left the callee reading
its arguments from uninitialised core registers.

Rebuild the mask for the non-struct CORE_STRUCT_CLASS case too, using the same
closed form as the struct arm, from THIS function's size (8 for a double, 4 for
a float) taken from VT_BTYPE and pplan->start: nw = min(size/4, 4 - start). The
size must come from VT_BTYPE, not type_size: type_size is the very function
MesCC mis-executes at runtime (it returns 4 for an 8-byte object -- the
struct-size bug that motivated patch 5), so a later "simplification" back to
type_size here would reintroduce the short mask. This restores the push-then-pop
{todo} marshalling that stock tcc uses for softfp doubles; a gcc-built tcc from
this source emits byte-identical code to the unpatched fork for these calls (the
push-then-pop sequence), so it is a faithful restoration, not a codegen change.

Note: this defect is specific to the two preceding copy_params patches in this
series (which introduced the discard-and-rebuild of *todo); stock upstream tcc
carries assign_regs' *todo through unchanged and is unaffected.
---
 arm-gen.c | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arm-gen.c b/arm-gen.c
--- a/arm-gen.c
+++ b/arm-gen.c
@@ -1232,6 +1232,24 @@ again:
                 stack_size -= pplan->prev->end - pplan->start; /* count that pad */
               }
             }
+            else if (i == CORE_STRUCT_CLASS) {
+              /* A softfp float/double assigned to core registers takes the
+                 is_float vpush path above (there is no VT_STRUCT store to hang
+                 the mask rebuild on), so its pop {todo} words must be recorded
+                 here too. assign_regs' *todo out-param was discarded at the top
+                 of copy_params (it is short under MesCC for the struct case), so
+                 EVERY CORE_STRUCT_CLASS member rebuilds its own mask; without
+                 this the vpushed doubles stay on the stack and r0-r3 are never
+                 loaded (bug19: 2+ softfp double args mispassed). Same closed
+                 form as the VT_STRUCT branch, from THIS size out of VT_BTYPE
+                 (8 for double, 4 for float) -- NOT type_size, the function
+                 MesCC mis-executes at runtime (do not simplify back to it). */
+              int nw = size >> 2;
+              if (pplan->start + nw > 4)
+                nw = 4 - pplan->start;
+              todo |= ((1 << (pplan->start + nw)) - 1) & ~((1 << pplan->start) - 1);
+              stack_size += size - 4 * nw; /* 0 unless it spills past r3 */
+            }
           }
           break;
 
